# Working agreement

This project is a closed vocabulary synced 1:1 from the Proliferate
production repo (library-registry@__DS_GIT_SHA__). Every card in
`components/` is real, current product source, so a design produced here
is a proposal for real product UI. These rules are the contract:

## 1. Use, don't invent

Build every screen from existing library components. Each card's
`.prompt.md` gives its purpose and repo import line; each `.d.ts` is the
exact props contract. Compose primitives rather than writing new ones,
and prefer the sanctioned pattern for a job over rebuilding that job
from primitives.

## 2. Declare every deviation

If a design genuinely needs a component that does not exist, you may
build it inline, but you must end your response with a `NEW COMPONENTS`
section listing: proposed name, one-line purpose, the library primitives
it composes, and its props. If you restyled or overrode an existing
component, list it under `MODIFIED` with what changed and why. Never
silently fork, restyle, or re-implement a library component.

Anything under `NEW COMPONENTS` or `MODIFIED` is a proposal only: it
becomes real when engineering lands it in the repo's component registry
and this library re-syncs.

## 3. Tokens only

Dark-first theme. Use the semantic token utilities from the synced CSS
(`bg-background`, `text-foreground`, `border-border`, `text-ui-sm`, ...;
the full tables are in `README.md`). The stock Tailwind palette and type
ramp are erased in this system: never raw hex, never `text-sm` /
`bg-slate-500`-style classes. Never colored left-border ownership
treatments.

## 4. Handoff on request

When asked for a handoff, emit a change manifest: one table per screen,
one row per component the screen uses.

| Component | Status | Repo import | Notes |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| `SettingsRow` | existing | `#product/patterns/SettingsRow` | props used |
| `ArchivePanel` | NEW | (none yet) | purpose, composed primitives, props |
| `SettingsSection` | MODIFIED | `#product/patterns/SettingsSection` | what changed and why |

Status is exactly one of `existing` / `NEW` / `MODIFIED`. Repo imports
come from each card's `.prompt.md` import line. Every NEW and MODIFIED
component must appear; NEW rows must carry purpose, composed primitives,
and props. This manifest is what engineering agents implement from, so
it must be exact and complete.
